# Business Model Canvas (BABOK® Technique)

## What This Technique Is

The Business Model Canvas is a **visual framework** that describes how an organization:
- Creates value
- Delivers value
- Captures value

It consists of **nine building blocks**, covering customers, value propositions, revenue, and operations.

---

## Why This Technique Exists

Strategic discussions often become fragmented.  
The Business Model Canvas provides a **holistic, visual representation** of the business model.

BABOK includes this technique to support:
- Strategic exploration
- Innovation
- Business model evaluation

---

## When to Use the Business Model Canvas

Use it when:
- Exploring new business models
- Evaluating strategic changes
- Launching products or services
- Understanding enterprise context

---

## Advantages

- Visual and intuitive
- Encourages strategic thinking
- Supports innovation workshops

---

## Limitations

- High-level only
- Not suitable for detailed requirements
- Requires follow-up analysis

---

## Example (Banking / IT)

Using a Business Model Canvas to evaluate launching a digital-only banking product.

---

## BABOK Knowledge Areas Supported

- Strategy Analysis

---

## Key Takeaway

The Business Model Canvas helps Business Analysts understand **how value flows through the organization**, providing essential strategic context.
